# The crew: one astronaut per player, one line per ship, in ship order.
# Edit names here and re-run tools/lvc.py; no code changes needed.
#
#   crew <name> ship <ship name> [quirk <quirk from fleet.lv>] [tag <word>]... [flagship]
#        [habit "<one sentence about {A}>"]
#
# Tags are optional flavour hooks for cards: `when tag A mech` only binds role A to crew
# carrying that tag. Use them to let a card *prefer* someone (pair it with an untagged
# twin), never to lock a whole storyline to one person. Tags never appear in card text.
#
# With no quirk, the astronaut's starting traits are seeded from the voyage key and
# their name, so they are stable from build to build but nobody picked them.
# Card text never assumes anyone's gender: use {A}/{B} or "they".
#
# Habits: one small, harmless, real detail per astronaut, sent in by that player and
# dropped in here. It is a whole sentence about {A}, e.g.
#   habit "{A} keeps one small thing from home within reach of the console."
# Cards marked `each crew` print the first habit (one clone per astronaut, compiled in;
# the phone never sees a new slot). Up to four habits per line: `each habit N` cards
# clone only for astronauts with a real Nth habit, so a quirk line only ever renders
# for its owner. Never invent a habit for a real person: leave it out (or leave the
# placeholder), and no clone is made. To add a ship, add one line here; the
# engine's crew count (lv/state.N, tools/lvc.py N_CREW) must match.

crew Phill     ship Ship 01   tag controls  flagship  habit "{A} keeps a pot of galley herbs alive under a spare lamp, pinching it back like the beds at home." habit "{A} fixes a loose locker hinge on the first try, then adds \"hinges\" to the house to-do list waiting on Earth." habit "Before every burn {A} writes one line on where everything stands, like a save before a hard level, in case anyone has to load from it."
crew Jacques   ship Ship 02   tag controls  habit "{A}'s kit is squared away past any inspection: straps dressed, pens taped, every call answered \"copy\" first." habit "{A} still checks a stock portfolio, on prices minutes old by the time they reach the ship. \"Long position,\" {A} says, and means the ship." habit "On entry eve {A} lays the suit out in donning order and runs the fleet's radio check in ninety crisp seconds."
crew Kim       ship Ship 03   tag controls  habit "{A} rations the episodes queued for the trip, one a week, and the fleet has learned not to call during one." habit "The water processor has a name, a rival and a tragic backstory now, courtesy of {A}, and the ground uses the name in tickets." habit "On the last corridor burn {A} allows the countdown one line of dramatic narration, then flies it dead straight."
crew Jai       ship Ship 04   tag controls  habit "{A} runs the hatch drill against a stopwatch and calls each module clear out loud, half a beat ahead of the checklist and never off it." habit "On the flyby plot {A} draws the trajectory as a racing line, apex marked. The nav team keeps the word." habit "{A} walks the entry timeline like a qualifying lap: the same marks, called aloud, every night, until the times stop changing."
crew Michelle  ship Ship 05   tag controls  habit "{A}'s mail from home carries a kitten count in the subject line, eleven one week, thirteen the next, one always out of frame." habit "{A} keeps a lint roller in the flight kit, a hundred million kilometres from any fur, and uses it before every call home." habit "Two days before entry, word reaches {A}: the last of the spring litter has gone to a home, and the house is briefly, suspiciously quiet."
crew Diego     ship Ship 06   tag mech  habit "{A} cat-proofs the cabin out of habit: cables clipped, nothing on a ledge, latches double-thrown. No cats aboard." habit "Mail from whoever is minding {A}'s two cats: both fed, both offended, one asleep in the bag {A} meant to pack." habit "{A} redraws a sagging locker bracket on a ration wrapper, lighter and stiffer; the ground files it as a drawing."
crew Dorian    ship Ship 07   tag controls  habit "A small boy at home keeps {A} in drawings: the ship, Mars and a dog, all the same size. {A} keeps every one." habit "{A} asks the ship's assistant to summarise the fault log. It answers in one confident paragraph; {A} checks every line." habit "The night before entry, a video: a Boston terrier at the front window, and a small voice telling it {A} is nearly there."
crew Marco     ship Ship 08   tag controls  habit "{A} builds the galley playlist for the week and times the coffee to land on the drop." habit "{A} finds the coolant pump cycling in four-four and builds the week's playlist around it. The ground's acoustic survey comes back marked allegro." habit "A photo reaches {A} from a dark, loud room: friends holding up a sign that says SAVING YOUR SPOT."
